{"error": null, "lastUpdated": 1778729369964, "loading": false, "notFound": false, "_id": "676edba19f7a5ed4f9d6e4bb", "authorID": "5f67899159b0841fe0d3891b", "boardID": "66ede8e631e33a29e8669bfa", "byID": null, "categoryID": null, "commentCount": 0, "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d", "deletedAt": null, "deletedBy": null, "details": "VRChat supports a range of languages, but only some worlds are multilingual. Having an example prefab that offers a UI with language options and a script that then goes over UI strings and replaces them would be great. Even better if it would load the strings from a JSON file or URL. It could use the SDK to detect game language and remember any overrides through persistence.\n\nCurrently I'm having problems finding a community made solution and I know world authors implement this manually.\n\nA prefab like this would incentivize world creators to implement multilingual support and seek translation contributions in their communities. Multilingual support should be considered a fundamental feature and I believe this fact makes it a great candidate for a new example prefab for Example Central.", "eta": null, "etaPublic": true, "fileURLs": [], "imageURLs": [], "maxScore": 17, "ogImageURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/og/58c62e995865713647a7115d/posts/676edba19f7a5ed4f9d6e4bb/1271425640.jpeg", "score": 17, "status": "open", "subCategoryID": null, "title": "Add a language switcher prefab", "trendingScore": 2936.441462929912, "updatedAt": "2026-05-14T03:31:44.837506Z", "updatedBy": null, "urlName": "add-a-language-switcher-prefab", "created": "2024-12-27T16:53:53.092Z", "statusChanged": "2024-12-27T16:53:53.092Z", "__v": 0, "ideaID": "680bba3ae4c3e90df139ec39", "viewerVote": 0, "linkedEntry": null, "board": {"_id": "66ede8e631e33a29e8669bfa", "name": "Example Central", "urlName": "example-central"}, "category": null, "voters": [{"_id": "6813c40754c640acaa0ca27e", "alias": "Sunglow Muskox", "aliasID": "6813c4088ccc1d8b3b43fbc9", "anony